{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1068734-do-sorcerers-still-exist-in-the-wod","id":1068734,"title":"Do sorcerers still exist in the WoD?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-03-27T10:19:43-07:00","id":1068734,"title":"Do sorcerers still exist in the WoD?","content":"M20 states that there are no longer any sorcerers among the Traditions, the Technocracy or the Disparate Alliance; all members (other than mortal acolytes) are Awakened mages. But what about the sorcerer groups found in Sorcerer Revised? The Maison Liban clearly have to go, since their whole shtick is that they are descended from sorcerers affiliated with House Tremere during the Dark Ages, but what about the other groups?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Our society is held together by the thinnest of threads: that exquisitely refined sense of tribal order.<br /> Edith Wharton, The Age of Innocence<br /> <br /> I am a huge fan of both the Trinity Universe and the classic World of Darkness.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12799-spellfire22","name":"Spellfire22","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T10:36:01-07:00","id":1068741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spellfire22</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1068734-do-sorcerers-still-exist-in-the-wod#post1068734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">M20 states that there are no longer any sorcerers among the Traditions, the Technocracy or the Disparate Alliance; all members (other than mortal acolytes) are Awakened mages. But what about the sorcerer groups found in Sorcerer Revised? The Maison Liban clearly have to go, since their whole shtick is that they are descended from sorcerers affiliated with House Tremere during the Dark Ages, but what about the other groups?</div> </div> </div> </div>Where does it say this?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T11:23:47-07:00","id":1068766,"title":"","content":"Hi Spellfire 22.<br /> <br /> M20 says this:<br /> <br /> According to the Revised edition of World of Darkness: Sorcerer, the Traditions now have unAwakened hedge magicians as well as Awakened mages among their ranks. Given the complexities and complications involved in hedge magic game systems, however, that merger has been ignored in Mage 20. If your individual troupe wants to feature sorcerers among the mages, go for it. The following chapters and rules do not address that subject \u2013 there\u2019s simply not enough room here to do justice to the idea.<br /> <br /> This doesn't mean a retcon. It simply means M20 does not cover the topic whatsoever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T11:36:11-07:00","id":1068771,"title":"","content":"To be a bit clearer with regards to this: You can run M20 by itself without any reference to outside material or hedge magicians among the Traditions. But, if you are going to use Sorcerers in the setting, M20 doesn't specifically state anything about them and how you are to use them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T11:36:32-07:00","id":1068772,"title":"","content":"Thanks, Spacecat! That definitely clarifies things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Our society is held together by the thinnest of threads: that exquisitely refined sense of tribal order.<br /> Edith Wharton, The Age of Innocence<br /> <br /> I am a huge fan of both the Trinity Universe and the classic World of Darkness.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12799-spellfire22","name":"Spellfire22","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T13:13:40-07:00","id":1068822,"title":"","content":"There are Numina/Hedge magic paths in Hunters Hunted II for V20 and I'll have some in the upcoming World of Darkness: Ghost Hunters book as well.<br /> <br /> Ghost Hunters is going to be useable across any/all of the *20 game lines (much like WoD: Mafia, WoD: Sorcerer were back in the previous editions).<br /> <br /> -MMM","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Owner/Editor - FlamesRising.com","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/949-matt-m-mcelroy","name":"Matt-M-McElroy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar949_2.jpeg","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T13:34:32-07:00","id":1068841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt-M-McElroy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1068734-do-sorcerers-still-exist-in-the-wod?p=1068822#post1068822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ghost Hunters is going to be useable across any/all of the *20 game lines (much like WoD: Mafia, WoD: Sorcerer were back in the previous editions).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm crazy excited about this one! I always loved the black cover World of Darkness books back in the day <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T19:47:42-07:00","id":1068992,"title":"","content":"It's sort of amusing that the 20th Anniversary follow-ups to the Year of the Hunter seem to skip over Werewolf and Mage entirely and go straight into Wraith... (^VVVVVV^)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T23:54:02-07:00","id":1069158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1068734-do-sorcerers-still-exist-in-the-wod?p=1068992#post1068992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's sort of amusing that the 20th Anniversary follow-ups to the Year of the Hunter seem to skip over Werewolf and Mage entirely and go straight into Wraith... (^VVVVVV^)</div> </div> </div> </div>I am not sure I'd count Paranormal investigators as Year of the Hunter. And I think HH2 basically covered the Werewolf groups.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T07:13:19-07:00","id":1069319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1068734-do-sorcerers-still-exist-in-the-wod?p=1069158#post1069158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am not sure I'd count Paranormal investigators as Year of the Hunter. And I think HH2 basically covered the Werewolf groups.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some of the groups, but everything is very much geared toward Vampire, with it being a V20 book and all. A book on Werewolf hunter groups would have to have DNA in it somewhere, and likely wouldn't make note of chaoscopes that cause the NSA to suddenly realize that there are ghosts and vampires all around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T08:45:24-07:00","id":1069385,"title":"","content":"There are linear mages in the groups, but m20 glosses over it for metaplot agnosticism and because sorcerer mechanics are kind of clunky. If you want them in, just treat them as mages that can only rote cast. Easiest way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T10:31:52-07:00","id":1069448,"title":"","content":"If you want your sorcerers to be significantly weaker than awakened mages without having to consult the Revised book on them. A quick way is to make all their magic require expenditure of Will Power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T10:54:58-07:00","id":1069466,"title":"","content":"I assume that sorcerers exist because as far as I'm concerned any major magical group, tradition or technocracy, it doesn't matter, wouldn't be able to exist without them. They're the middle managers that keep the organization running, keeping an eye on the unawakened members and allowing mages to focus on the big decisions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T17:45:41-07:00","id":1069742,"title":"","content":"Personally, I don't much like the sorcery mechanics as they are. While I don't really deal with them much personally, this is the way I'd handle that kind of linear magic.<br /> <br /> Say Harry the Hermetic wants to be able to teach some sleepers to be able to fly. But they're not awakened. So what does he do? He goes about creating the 'Path of Flight' using the rules for a Talisman. The path of flight is a Arete X talisman (Generally very high.) That includes three effects. Firstly, it allows someone with access to it to use it to cast the spell 'fly' by using the methods described by the path. Secondly, it allows a current user to enable a new user, (without losing their user status) by forging a correspondence link between the Path and the new student of flight.<br /> <br /> There. You have flying mortals. The same can be done with any set of powers you can think of. Schools of sorcery would have access to whatever powers the mages aligned with them could think up and develop a path for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T21:52:27-07:00","id":1069864,"title":"","content":"Incidentally, I devised an alternative to the current sorcery system here and a variant on the next page.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1067073-cleaning-up-the-clutter-of-the-wod-psychics-are-just-wild-talented-orphans?_=1490762954308\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1067073-cleaning-up-the-clutter-of-the-wod-psychics-are-just-wild-talented-orphans?_=1490762954308\"> Cleaning up the clutter of the WoD: Psychics are just Wild Talented Orphans - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1067073-cleaning-up-the-clutter-of-the-wod-psychics-are-just-wild-talented-orphans?_=1490762954308\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1067073-cleaning-up-the-clutter-of-the-wod-psychics-are-just-wild-talented-orphans?_=1490762954308 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> So Psychics in the WoD irk me. They feel out of place. They don't jive with any game other than Hunter, and there the issue is that they are overshadowed by Mystical Numina, which they clash with. A small tweak in psychics fix them, in my opinion. Psychics are Awakened individuals, Orphans, with Wild Talent and little idea of their powers. Pyrokinesis? Forces. Can he move objects? No. &amp;quot;My powers don't work that way.&amp;quot; Now, this limitation is purely psychological, and with the right placebo (I will use my ancient powers to overcome your mental block, for example) or use of Mind could open </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T23:22:24-07:00","id":1069903,"title":"","content":"Basically, Mage already has a magic system, and doesn't need two where one player is going to quickly power past the other","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T07:26:09-07:00","id":1070048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1068734-do-sorcerers-still-exist-in-the-wod?p=1069466#post1069466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I assume that sorcerers exist because as far as I'm concerned any major magical group, tradition or technocracy, it doesn't matter, wouldn't be able to exist without them. They're the middle managers that keep the organization running, keeping an eye on the unawakened members and allowing mages to focus on the big decisions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorcerers are also important for the purpose of passing knowledge down through the generations, especially if Awakened recruits are sparse. Game mechanics aside, the Focus of a given group is largely the same, regardless of whether the members of that group are Awakened or not. Hermetic Sorcerers draw the same magic circles, Choristers sing the same hymns, Akashics all learn Do as a martial art/lifestyle, etc. It's just that Mages can take the same methods as their Sorcerer compatriots, and take them farther.<br /> <br /> The Verbana in particular makes extensive use of Sorcery, as family lines pass knowledge of the Old Ways down the generations, from parent to child. As it's unlikely for each generation to produce an individual that will Awaken, Sorcery becomes the default assumption among these families. Any family member who does Awaken is considered particularly talented or gifted, and is provided with all the old spell books and items that only they could properly use. The fundamental framework of witchcraft, however, is taught as a matter of course. Same with the Order of Hermes, where High Sorcery is considered standard curriculum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T08:51:32-07:00","id":1070119,"title":"","content":"See, my problem with that is primers exist. Meaning you can teach Awakening.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T09:23:42-07:00","id":1070145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1068734-do-sorcerers-still-exist-in-the-wod?p=1070119#post1070119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See, my problem with that is primers exist. Meaning you can teach Awakening.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but even with a Primer awakening is not guaranteed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T09:42:20-07:00","id":1070159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1068734-do-sorcerers-still-exist-in-the-wod?p=1070119#post1070119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See, my problem with that is primers exist. Meaning you can teach Awakening.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's possible to induce Awakening. That doesn't mean it's guaranteed, even with a Primer. Not everyone who reads a Primer will &quot;get it&quot;, and not every reader will try. Some are diametrically opposed to the world view espoused by a given Primer, and actively resist internalizing its lessons (assuming they bother to finish reading it). Some Primers are just so dense, abstract, and <i>old</i> that it takes real effort and additional scholarship to grasp the meaning.<br /> <br /> When I say &quot;old&quot;, I mean the Primers were written centuries or even millennia ago, and in contexts that modern readers may have trouble grasping. Even if we assume a Primer has been translated (which takes a great deal of effort to do, while allowing the text to retain its enchantment), words may change dramatically in accepted meaning between one generation, let alone the historical time scales we're working with. The Kitab Al-Alacir is one of the most widely used Primers, not because it's any more effective than other Primers in Awakening people, but because it's been the beneficiary of numerous successful translations. If a translation hasn't been &quot;updated&quot; in a century, though, the meaning behind word choices could be lost to anyone who isn't familiar with the old contexts with which those words were used. Or, more simply, dedicated scholars of obscure linguistics.<br /> <br /> Indeed, many groups don't translate their Primers into more accessible languages at all. Partly because it's difficult to do so while not &quot;breaking&quot; the enchantment on the text. And partly because they may decide that only the truly dedicated and educated should be trusted with Awakening, if it can be helped. It's the same reason why Hermetic education involves learning several languages - only someone with the force of Will needed to jump through their hoops should be allowed access to their magic.<br /> <br /> The various mage groups also likely keep careful control about how their Primers are distributed. Sure, it's the Text and not the medium it's written on that makes a Primer, but there are dangers to letting that Text proliferate too widely. If anyone on the street could get their hands on the Kitab Al-Alacir, for instance, it would mean that anyone on the street could potentially Awaken...in a setting where the Traditions or other groups would not know about it. That person could end up being picked up by the Technocracy - or the Nephandi - bolstering the ranks of the Traditions' enemies. At least when folks like Society of Ether hand a copy to hopeful recruits, there's the understanding that if it doesn't work out, the text can be retrieved or destroyed later. To release a copy of a Primer out into the world, with no controls in place, is a risk. And if they're going to do it, it must be a calculated risk.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T13:34:17-07:00","id":1070267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1068734-do-sorcerers-still-exist-in-the-wod?p=1070145#post1070145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True, but even with a Primer awakening is not guaranteed.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's all but guaranteed though. It takes someone rather special to be so dense that even a primer won't shock them awake. Though Bluecho is right that Primers generally require active study, that doesn't translate to &quot;Mages are so rare that we need a whole other splat just to pass on the traditions.&quot;<br /> <br /> Also, it is my understanding that the process of reading a primer and internalizing it's lessons actually sets the students paradigm. So while yes, Nephandi or the Technocracy could convert them later, The same could be said of literally any student.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T15:08:10-07:00","id":1070325,"title":"","content":"Eh...well, to read any Grimoire, including these, you need to be receptive to the Paradigm. This does not mean that the Paradigm it's &quot;settled&quot;, but merely that a guy that doesn't believe somewhat in the occult would be less receptive to a Hermetic Premier than a member of the Golden Down","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T02:53:44-07:00","id":1070547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FbDF p. 68</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Sleeper must be of above average intellect and willing (even if only subconsciously) to open his mind to new ways of perceiving the world. If the Sleeper reads the entire Primer and makes an active attempt to understand the contents, he will most likely Awaken.</div> </div> </div> </div>Quite some requirements. Even if you fulfill all of them, you might not Awaken.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T03:42:11-07:00","id":1070554,"title":"","content":"Man... that would really suck if you and a study partner studied one of these primers together for a decade in the exact same way, trading ideas, and sharing mind opening practices and at the end of it the other guy awakens. It'd be like &quot;I'm so happy for you...&quot; (Hide and cry)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T06:03:40-07:00","id":1070597,"title":"","content":"Why is it that when a sorcerer thread comes up most people treat them as &quot;lesser mages&quot;?<br /> <br /> They have defined powers and full mention in multiple books from other games-lines (hunters hunted, demon hunter x, project twilight...) and sorcerer's first book was a crossover book that, while heavily flawed by rushed production, lack of editors, and vague writing, put fifth-dot sorcerers at similar level to other supernaturals at the same power(heck the original write up for shape-shifting made it one of the best powers to have in WOD at the time it was released).<br /> <br /> Even with revised tying them to mage, it still seems like looking at the kue-jin as lesser vampires with eastern flavor or mummies as egyptian lesser risen to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T06:12:20-07:00","id":1070598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1068734-do-sorcerers-still-exist-in-the-wod?p=1070597#post1070597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why is it that when a sorcerer thread comes up most people treat them as &amp;quot;lesser mages&amp;quot;?<br /> <br /> They have defined powers and full mention in multiple books from other games-lines (hunters hunted, demon hunter x, project twilight...) and sorcerer's first book was a crossover book that, while heavily flawed by rushed production, lack of editors, and vague writing, put fifth-dot sorcerers at similar level to other supernaturals at the same power(heck the original write up for shape-shifting made it one of the best powers to have in WOD at the time it was released).<br /> <br /> Even with revised tying them to mage, it still seems like looking at the kue-jin as lesser vampires with eastern flavor or mummies as egyptian lesser risen to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>To say it thoughtfully and with respect:<br /> Because they are.<br /> <br /> At least from a certain angle, eyes squinted, in the dark.<br /> <br /> On surface they are less versatile and are not as elitist as mages. Because of numbers.<br /> An awakened Mage is special by rarity.<br /> Sorcerers combined outnumber Mages (and most other splats, too) several times over.<br /> (Depending on source, headcanon, etc.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T06:28:38-07:00","id":1070608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1068734-do-sorcerers-still-exist-in-the-wod?p=1070598#post1070598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To say it thoughtfully and with respect:<br /> Because they are.<br /> <br /> At least from a certain angle, eyes squinted, in the dark.<br /> <br /> On surface they are less versatile and are not as elitist as mages. Because of numbers.<br /> An awakened Mage is special by rarity.<br /> Sorcerers combined outnumber Mages (and most other splats, too) several times over.<br /> (Depending on source, headcanon, etc.)</div> </div> </div> </div>All other supernaturals are less versatile than mages and most supernaturals outnumber mages save particularly rare ones, so that isn't saying much.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't say sorcerers outnumber most supernaturals either, humans with numina yes, but while all sorcerers are humans with numina not all humans with numina are sorcerers(there are also ghouls, revenants, kinfolk, kinian, cyborgs, &quot;true faith&quot; mortals, thralls, etc...). Neither sorcerer books address numbers of sorcerers as apposed to vampires or garou to my knowledge so it'd be mostly head-canon anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T07:06:45-07:00","id":1070618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1068734-do-sorcerers-still-exist-in-the-wod?p=1070597#post1070597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why is it that when a sorcerer thread comes up most people treat them as &quot;lesser mages&quot;?<br /> <br /> They have defined powers and full mention in multiple books from other games-lines (hunters hunted, demon hunter x, project twilight...) and sorcerer's first book was a crossover book that, while heavily flawed by rushed production, lack of editors, and vague writing, put fifth-dot sorcerers at similar level to other supernaturals at the same power(heck the original write up for shape-shifting made it one of the best powers to have in WOD at the time it was released).<br /> <br /> Even with revised tying them to mage, it still seems like looking at the kue-jin as lesser vampires with eastern flavor or mummies as egyptian lesser risen to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, mechanically speaking, if you check what a starting mage can do,say with 3 dots in 3 spheres (say for example Correspondence &amp; Entropy) you will get someone with far more powers than your typical starting sorcerer. (Sense space including distances &amp; direction; something like Clairvoyance at 5 dots; something like Conveyance with range better than 6; speed 5, and number 2; The teleport ward ritual; Something like Divination with time at 4ish, Accuracy 5ish, &amp; Question 5ish; Something Like Fortune with all aspects at 5ish or better). This happens for pretty much any sphere and some spheres combo to give the mage even more powers.<br /> <br /> And since they are both more or less humans with magic, this makes the sorcerers seem a lot like lesser mages, mage in general fantasy parlance outside of the WoD being a magic user.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12480,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","user":"Spacecat","date":". 03-30-2017, 10:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T07:18:24-07:00","id":1070623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacecat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1068734-do-sorcerers-still-exist-in-the-wod?p=1070618#post1070618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, mechanically speaking, if you check what a starting mage can do,say with 3 dots in 3 spheres (say for example Correspondence &amp; Entropy) you will get someone with far more powers than your typical starting sorcerer. (Sense space including distances &amp; direction; something like Clairvoyance at 5 dots; something like Conveyance with range better than 6; speed 5, and number 2; The teleport ward ritual; Something like Divination with time at 4ish, Accuracy 5ish, &amp; Question 5ish; Something Like Fortune with all aspects at 5ish or better). This happens for pretty much any sphere and some spheres combo to give the mage even more powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, the same could be said with a starting mage vs any starting supernatural. Mages can be OP if played right, they have their own system of rules without any real functional limit. Does that make a vampire a lesser mage? maybe only in a mage game. Sorcerers aren't solely a mage supernatural as they appear fully stated in vampire and werewolf books as well(actually having sorcerer paths while mages in said books tend to have powers based on the gameline).<br /> <br /> Maybe it's a like mages paradigms in how I think of sorcerers as another supernatural entirely(like the difference between a vampire and a kue-jin) when others see them as mortals trying to be mages(like a vampire to a ghoul)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T07:19:14-07:00","id":1070624,"title":"","content":"In Mage, Magic(k) rullz, and all other supernaturals don't understand a thing about how the world trully works. Sorcerers were invented for Vampire to give hunters a mistical edge, and then poorly adapted to Mage as some sort of not-really mages that never do anything whorty to mention in the big scheme of the Metaplot.<br /> You gota live with it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 03-30-2017, 10:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T07:58:26-07:00","id":1070639,"title":"","content":"on sorcerers, wondered a bit, how to reflect a diviner antaganists divinations in a way that is worthy, but doesnt &quot;auto kill&quot; PC's.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T08:33:04-07:00","id":1070665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1068734-do-sorcerers-still-exist-in-the-wod?p=1070623#post1070623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, the same could be said with a starting mage vs any starting supernatural. Mages can be OP if played right, they have their own system of rules without any real functional limit. Does that make a vampire a lesser mage? maybe only in a mage game. Sorcerers aren't solely a mage supernatural as they appear fully stated in vampire and werewolf books as well(actually having sorcerer paths while mages in said books tend to have powers based on the gameline).</div> </div> </div> </div>What I'm saying is that people tend to directly compare a Mage (Reality bending Magic user) to a Sorcerer (User of magical paths). Furthermore, sorcerers can awaken to become mages. In the setting of the game, one can hardly even see the difference between the two except that one is more supernaturally versatile and powerful. (They both are more or less indistinguishable from normal people and both say magic words, use magic gestures, and do magical feats)<br /> <br /> People tend to classify the stuff other supernaturals do as &quot;Vampire Powers&quot; or &quot;Werewolf Powers&quot; and such because you generally can't do these unless you are a vampire or werewolf or the like. They don't consider these magic in the same sense as a mage's or sorcerer's magic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1068734-do-sorcerers-still-exist-in-the-wod?p=1070623#post1070623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe it's a like mages paradigms in how I think of sorcerers as another supernatural entirely(like the difference between a vampire and a kue-jin) when others see them as mortals trying to be mages(like a vampire to a ghoul)</div> </div> </div> </div>It's that, a matter of perspective. You just seem to see the more text and numeric mechanic side of things and not what these guys represent to most people. They are, after all, just rules of a game, but people like to view them as representations of something else. It just so happens that mages and sorcerers more or less represent the same sort of thing to most people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12480,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","user":"Spacecat","date":". 03-30-2017, 11:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T08:38:19-07:00","id":1070669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1068734-do-sorcerers-still-exist-in-the-wod?p=1070639#post1070639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">on sorcerers, wondered a bit, how to reflect a diviner antaganists divinations in a way that is worthy, but doesnt &quot;auto kill&quot; PC's.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really inept minions! Probably not the answer you are looking for though.<br /> <br /> I think the best way to do this is to play out, at least in your head, exactly what your diviner does &quot;In-game&quot; as a person, including divination rolls, figuring out the information they are most interested in, the questions they will ask with their divinations, how much time they devote to things each day, and how they use their resources to further their goals with this knowledge in mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T09:10:42-07:00","id":1070684,"title":"","content":"I dont a black spiral dancer pack qualifys as &quot;Minions&quot; of a kinfolk sorcerer","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/189